[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue ("the parser reads dates month first"). The
reports say otherwise. Read by tenant locale and booking form, they hold three problems, and one
fix does not close them all.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Three tickets, filed in the
[mega-s01e03-4471](https://github.com/mperazac/mega-s01e03-4471/issues) repo.
</Callout>

## The problems

1. **Parser reads dates month first** ([issue 1](https://github.com/mperazac/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/1)).
   Day-first tenants get flipped dates. This is the cause #4471 names, and the largest group.
2. **booking-v3 shows `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field** ([issue 2](https://github.com/mperazac/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/2)).
   Day-first tenants on that form type month first, as the hint tells them. This is a form bug, so the
   parser fix will not close it.
3. **Bookings move by one day** ([issue 3](https://github.com/mperazac/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/3)).
   Five reports describe a one-day shift, not a month and day swap. Suspected time zone bug, not
   confirmed. The table below files them under `parser`, as the desk did (`desk-notes.json`).

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts by cause in the code. Problem 3 sits inside the `parser` row, so the issue counts
are 374 for problem 1 and 5 for problem 3.

## Why the intake tag misled us

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser. That is a guess, and it disagrees with the cause
often: the table's "tagged as" column shows it. Read the tenant's locale and form instead.

